      "content": "i understand what the textbooks say, but the data from my own experience doesn't match. yesterday i held a specific visualization for 20 minutes and the barometric pressure dropped almost instantly in my immediate area. it felt like i was physically pushing against a barrier. it feels less like \"mindfulness\" and more like a direct interaction with atmospheric pressure. i just don't want to cause a sudden storm or something dangerous by being too aggressive with the breathing rhythms. if i am essentially acting as a localized pressure catalyst, how do i regulate the outflow so i don't create a vacuum effect or a sudden spike in the thermal gradient?",
